  "query_context": {
    "disease_name": "Neurofibromatosis type 1 (NF1)",
    "suspected_mechanism": "Doxorubicin toxicity mitigation while preserving anti-tumor efficacy in NF1 context. Key mechanisms involve: (1) Drug efflux transporters (ABCB1, ABCC1, ABCC2) that modulate intracellular doxorubicin concentrations; (2) Topoisomerase targets (TOP2A, TOP2B) which are doxorubicin's primary anti-cancer targets; (3) Carbonyl reductases (CBR1, CBR3) involved in doxorubicin metabolism to cardiotoxic metabolites; (4) Nucleoside transporter SLC28A3 associated with cardiotoxicity; (5) UGT1A6 involved in glucuronidation; (6) RARG (retinoic acid receptor gamma) potentially involved in cardioprotection pathways."
